From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:11:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 453/488] [DS4.1] Sampler-side glue in TileLang: Gumbel finish,
 row clears, draft gather

- Gumbel-max sampling's finish (torch's argmax over the blocks and the
  gather of the winner) as one warp-a-token kernel, torch.argmax's order.
- The penalties' bincount rows cleared in one launch (an int64 cast and
  two index_fill_ before).
- The thinking budget's marker caches reset in one launch (three
  index_fill_ before).
- The consumed drafts gathered into a persistent buffer for the
  scheduler's grammar check (an ATen index before).
---
